<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO HG upgrades Wegener to Buy.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO HG upgrades Wegener to Buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary Feb 19 research note.</p>
<p>    Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Wegener	   Publishing    190     ABN AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>COMMENT: Upgraded to Buy from Hold. Share price target 210. Restructuring potential of traditional publishing operations, exposure to high-growth, high-margin direct marketing business and potential fruits of Arcade record labels will contribute to compound annual earnings growth of 10 pct. From an international perspective Wegener's valuation is undemanding at 1998 EV/EBITDA multiple of 5.6. Discounted cashflow valuation suggests share price can reach 210 guilders.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    Cashflow   P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996		  10.26   18.5   18.55	10.2   3.60</p>
<p>    1997		  11.75   16.2   21.34	8.9    4.10</p>
<p>    1998		  13.40   14.2   23.71	8.0    4.70</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
